      ":question/problem": "Express $\\sin\\left(\\theta+2\\pi\\right)$ in terms of $\\sin \\theta$ and $\\cos \\theta$.\n\nUse the formula\n\n$$\n\\sin(u+v)=\\sin u\\cos v+\\cos u\\sin v\n$$\n\nand the exact values $\\cos\\left(2\\pi\\right)=1$ and $\\sin\\left(2\\pi\\right)=0$.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Use the sum formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\sin(u+v)=\\sin u\\cos v+\\cos u\\sin v.\n$$\n\nThe fixed angle has exact values\n\n$$\n\\cos\\left(2\\pi\\right)=1,\\qquad \\sin\\left(2\\pi\\right)=0.\n$$\n\nSubstitute $u=\\theta$ and $v=2\\pi$, then simplify the coefficients:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\sin\\left(\\theta+2\\pi\\right)&=\\sin \\theta\\cos\\left(2\\pi\\right)+\\cos \\theta\\sin\\left(2\\pi\\right)\\\\\n&=\\sin \\theta\\left(1\\right)+\\cos \\theta\\left(0\\right)\\\\\n&=\\sin \\theta.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
